--[[
`coroutine.sus.cancellation` identifies cancellation within one Lua state.

```nupp
local cancellation = coroutine.sus.cancellation
local stopped = cancellation.create("read", "closed")
assert(cancellation.is(stopped))
```

`create` produces the cancellation value shared by suspension, structured tasks,
and worker adapters. `is` recognizes its metatable identity without relying on
message text. The operation and optional reason remain available as fields, and
string conversion produces a contextual cancellation message.

Runtime implementations load this helper without initializing the
[](coroutine.sus) facade. They share its cancellation identity throughout one
Lua state.

Worker states reconstruct cancellation values locally; no metatable or Lua
object identity is transferred between states.
]]
module coroutine.sus.cancellation

local source1 = require("nupp.suspension.cancellation")
export const create = source1.create
export const is = source1.is
